Based on that page, the paymentservice-a MCP server uses the SSE (Server-Sent Events) / MCP V2 protocol. The server returns `allow: POST` for `GET` requests, which tells you that SSE is the transport — the proper endpoint is `https://paymentservice-a.companyone.example.com/mcp-v2`.

To add it to your `pi` configs (which in Claude Code/Agent context is typically `~/.claude/claude_desktop_config.json` or `~/.claude/config.json`):

**Option 1: `claude_desktop_config.json`**
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "paymentservice-a": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": [
        "@anthropic-ai/claude-code-bridge",
        "mcp",
        "sse",
        "https://paymentservice-a.companyone.example.com/mcp-v2"
      ],
      "env": {}
    }
  }
}
```

**Option 2: Direct SSE config (`~/.claude/config.json`)**
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "paymentservice-a": {
      "url": "https://paymentservice-a.companyone.example.com/mcp-v2",
      "type": "sse"
    }
  }
}
```

**Option 3: If you just want the bare SSE endpoint**
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "paymentservice-a": {
      "command": "curl",
      "args": [
        "-N",
        "-H",
        "Accept: application/json",
        "-H",
        "Content-Type: application/json",
        "https://paymentservice-a.companyone.example.com/mcp-v2"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

The exact config format depends on which "pi configs" tool you're using (Claude Desktop, Claude Code, or a different MCP runner). The key detail is that it's an `https://` SSE endpoint accepting POST requests.

